---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const patchUrl = `${base}/patches/tongari-boushi-en-v2.32-rev1-test.xdelta`;
const patchSize = '3.10 MB';
const patchSha256 = '8992d021e5e1e1cfa2ea17198c81807ac0f1d04d83186f88c9ed9a73382736bb';
const patchedRomSha256 = '1bda3c9cab336554dca91c8403b2417ece512becf6aed585eed8528eff068f20';
---

<Layout title="v2.32 Rev 1 test build">
  <!-- NOTE: this page is unlinked from the rest of the site.
       Header.astro nav does not include /test/. Patches page does not
       reference v2.32-rev1-test. It is reachable only by direct URL. -->
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Tongari Boushi v2.32 — Rev 1 test build</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Test build for Freedom. Not the public release.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card download-card">
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <a class="big-button" href={patchUrl} download>
      tongari-boushi-en-v2.32-rev1-test.xdelta&nbsp;
      <span class="size">({patchSize})</span>
    </a>
    <dl class="meta">
      <dt>Source ROM</dt>
      <dd>JP <strong>Rev 1</strong> (filename usually ends with <code>(J) Rev 1.nds</code>)</dd>
      <dt>Patch SHA-256</dt>
      <dd><code>{patchSha256}</code></dd>
      <dt>Patched ROM SHA-256 (what you should get out)</dt>
      <dd><code>{patchedRomSha256}</code></dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>What's in this build</h2>
    <p class="intro">
      Every bullet below is byte-verified against the produced ROM.
      Full report:
      <code>notes/_v232_clean_rev1_verified_changes.md</code> in the
      translation repo.
    </p>
    <ul class="changes">
      <li>
        <strong>Fish-catch screens no longer make you press through 16 blank dialog pages.</strong>
        Every "You caught a ___!" message (Pacific Saury, Flounder,
        Crab, Sea Robin, Yellowtail, and 17 others — 22 entries in
        <code>msg99051.ofs</code> 66–87) had a trailing run of 16
        empty phrase boundaries plus a stray <code>*</code> character.
        All 22 now end cleanly on the result line.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Routine NPC dialogs no longer flash an extra blank page mid-line.</strong>
        About 7,899 dialog entries had a leftover empty phrase
        boundary that made you press A through an extra blank dialog
        box. Those now advance directly. 555 had two leftover
        boundaries; those are also fixed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Internal placeholder-leakage regression cannot ship from this pipeline again.</strong>
        The prior v2.32 candidate had 4,350 literal placeholder tokens
        (<code>[NPC_DAT:</code>, <code>[PLAYER_NAME]</code>, etc.)
        leaking into ROM bytes as visible text. The build pipeline now
        has a byte-level gate that scans every produced <code>.nds</code>
        for those patterns and refuses to release if any are found.
        This build has 0 leaks.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Everything from v2.31 still works as it did.</strong>
        All 40 sentinels pass: 29 song retranslations (Summer Cottage,
        Broken Tears, Congasta, etc.), the His Majesty canon (58
        occurrences), Berry's shop (378 occurrences), the leading-§
        strip on the 10 affected entries, the Her Majesty ban (0
        occurrences), and the v2.31 stability fixes (friend menu,
        sing/hum codec, clothing codec, bug-registering crash) all
        stay applied byte-for-byte.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Verification</h2>
    <p>This build passed all three production integrity gates:</p>
    <ul class="gates">
      <li><strong>Sentinels — 40 / 40 passed.</strong> Every invariant
        from v2.31 (His Majesty count, song retranslations, leading-§
        strip, ban list) verified against the rebuilt ROM.</li>
      <li><strong>Rebuild gate — 34 / 34 fix-manifest rows present.</strong>
        Every row of every fix manifest had its <code>after_value</code>
        substring located in the rebuilt ROM bytes.</li>
      <li><strong>Placeholder-leakage gate — 0 leaks.</strong> Byte
        scan of the entire 268,435,456-byte ROM for literal
        placeholder text turned up nothing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta-hash">
      Patched-ROM SHA-256: <code>{patchedRomSha256}</code>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>How to apply</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Get the JP <strong>Rev 1</strong> ROM of <em>Tongari Boushi to
        Oshare na Mahou Tsukai</em>. The filename usually ends in
        <code>(J) Rev 1.nds</code>. Confirm with an MD5 / SHA256 of the
        clean dump if you have one to compare against.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use <a href="https://www.romhacking.net/utilities/704/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delta Patcher</a>
        (or any xdelta3-compatible tool):
        <ul class="bare">
          <li>Original file → your JP Rev 1 ROM</li>
          <li>XDelta patch → the <code>.xdelta</code> downloaded above</li>
          <li>Apply</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
        The output should be a 268,435,456-byte <code>.nds</code> with
        SHA-256 <code>1bda3c9c…</code> (full hash above). If you don't
        see that hash, the source ROM is the wrong revision or got
        corrupted.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted small">
      Equivalent command-line: <code>xdelta3 -d -s &lt;jp-rev1.nds&gt; tongari-boushi-en-v2.32-rev1-test.xdelta &lt;out.nds&gt;</code>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 40px 0 12px;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 1.9rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 64ch;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .card {
    background: var(--surface-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-pink-100);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
    padding: 24px 28px;
    margin: 22px 0;
  }

  .card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-purple-600);
  }

  .download-card {
    text-align: left;
  }

  .big-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 14px 22px;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-pink-400), var(--color-purple-400));
    color: white;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1rem;
    box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(155, 123, 217, 0.25);
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  .big-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(155, 123, 217, 0.35);
    color: white;
  }

  .big-button .size {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .meta {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: 6px 16px;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .meta dt {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .meta dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .meta code {
    font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--color-purple-600);
    background: var(--color-purple-50);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    word-break: break-all;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-purple-100);
  }

  .intro {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .changes {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .changes li {
    margin: 12px 0;
  }

  .changes li::marker {
    color: var(--color-pink-400);
  }

  .changes strong {
    color: var(--color-purple-600);
  }

  .not-in {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    background: var(--color-purple-50);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-purple-400);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .gates {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 22px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .gates li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }

  .gates strong {
    color: var(--color-pink-600);
  }

  .meta-hash {
    margin: 14px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .meta-hash code {
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  ol {
    padding-left: 22px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  ol li {
    margin: 8px 0;
  }

  .bare {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin: 6px 0;
  }

  .bare li {
    margin: 2px 0;
  }

  .muted {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .small {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  code {
    font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.88em;
    background: var(--color-purple-50);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: var(--color-purple-600);
  }
</style>
